Patient-Robot Instructions: Physical AI Oncology Trials
======================================================
LaTeX Source Code and Compiled PDF — v1.9.1

Files
-----
- patient_robot_instructions.tex   Main LaTeX document (10 pages)
- patient_robot_instructions.sty   Custom style package
- references.bib                   BibTeX bibliography (28 references)
- README                           This file

Compilation
-----------
To compile the LaTeX source:

    pdflatex patient_robot_instructions.tex
    bibtex patient_robot_instructions
    pdflatex patient_robot_instructions.tex
    pdflatex patient_robot_instructions.tex

Or with latexmk:

    latexmk -pdf patient_robot_instructions.tex

Requirements: texlive-latex-base, texlive-latex-extra, texlive-fonts-recommended

Note: Images are in ../images/ (numbered 1.png through 10.png).

Note on Images
--------------
Images are sourced from the Google Drive folder:
https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Cpe7fz3KlaERIfd6LQz2wmSBQNmB00Ax

To reproduce the full PDF with illustrations, run:

    python3 patients/generate_pdf.py

PDF Versions
------------
Three PDF versions are generated:
  - Full size (original image quality)
  - 10 MB target (optimized images)
  - 5 MB target (compressed images)

Content Overview
----------------
10 pages, each a self-contained instructional sheet for one robot type:

  Page 1:  Surgical Robots (prostate cancer)
  Page 2:  Cobots / Collaborative Robots (breast cancer)
  Page 3:  Radiotherapy Patient-Positioning Robots (lung cancer)
  Page 4:  Robotic Needle-Placement Systems (liver cancer)
  Page 5:  Social Companion Robots — Pediatric (leukemia)
  Page 6:  Humanoids — Pediatric (bone cancer)
  Page 7:  Radiotherapy Motion-Management / Tracking Robots (pancreatic cancer)
  Page 8:  Imaging Assistant Robots (thyroid cancer)
  Page 9:  Steerable Needle / Needle-Steering Robots (kidney cancer)
  Page 10: Rehabilitation Exoskeletons / Robotic Gait Trainers (bone cancer post-surgery)

Each page includes:
  (a) Header: Author, ORCID, affiliation, email
  (b) Title: "Patient-Robot Instructions: AI Oncology Trials - [Robot Type]"
  (c) Image: New illustration from Google Drive (largest portion of page)
  (d) Dashed horizontal bar, robot type full name, bold bar
  (e) One introductory sentence + 3-item numbered list (quantitative interaction data)
  (f) Footer: Date, DOI, AI model, page number, sources, "For Demonstration Purposes Only"

